style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:5.85pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;position:relative;top:-3.15pt;vertical-align:baseline"&gt;a.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:13.13pt"&gt;ONEOK Rockies Midstream, L.L.C. (ONEOK Rockies), is a subsidiary of ONEOK Inc.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0d2e82;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;9.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0d2e82;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt; TRANSACTIONS WITH RELATED PARTIES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The day-to-day management of the Partnership&#8217;s affairs is the responsibility of TransCanada Northern Border, Inc., a wholly owned subsidiary of TC Energy, (TransCanada Northern Border) pursuant to an operating &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;agreement between TransCanada Northern Border and the Partnership effective April 1, 2007 (as amended). TransCanada Northern Border utilizes the services of TC Energy and its affiliates for management services related to the Partnership. The Partnership is charged for the capital, salaries, benefits and expenses of TC Energy and its affiliates attributable to the Partnership's operations. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, costs charged to the Partnership are summarized in the following table:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:64.434%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:59.639%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.530%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.531%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #0a2299;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #0a2299;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="6" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;(In thousands)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;Costs charged to TC Energy's subsidiaries:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 13pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;Capital costs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;12,919&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9,989&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 13pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;Operating costs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;35,729&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;36,738&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;At December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Partnership owed $1.3 million and $1.4 million, respectively, from these related parties. These amounts are reported under Accounts Payable to Associated Companies (234) on the balance sheets net of Accounts Receivable from Associated Companies (146) on the Partnership's balance sheet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Partnership had contracted firm capacity held by two customers affiliated with the Partnership&#8217;s general partners, namely ONEOK Rockies, a subsidiary of ONEOK Inc. and beginning in November 2020, TC Energy Marketing, Inc (TC Energy Marketing), a wholly owned subsidiary of TC Energy. For the year ended December 31, 2025, revenue and outstanding receivable from TC Energy Marketing are $3.7 million and $0.4 million, respectively. Additionally, the Partnership entered into a transportation agreement with ANR Pipeline Company (ANR), a TC Energy affiliate, to provide ANR with 203,600 Dth/day of capacity from November 2027 through October 2047 on the Partnership's pipeline system. See Note 8, Transactions with Major Customers, for details regarding revenues and outstanding accounts receivable balances with ONEOK Rockies for the past two years.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0d2e82;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;(10) CASH DISTRIBUTION AND CONTRIBUTION POLICY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Partnership&#8217;s General Partnership Agreement provides that distributions to its partners are to be made on a pro rata basis according to each partner&#8217;s capital account balance. The Partnership&#8217;s Management Committee has the responsibility to determine the amount and timing of the distributions to its partners including equity contributions and the funding of growth capital expenditures. In addition, any inability to refinance maturing debt will be funded by equity contributions. Any changes to, or suspension of, the Partnership&#8217;s cash distribution policy requires the unanimous approval of the Management Committee. The Partnership&#8217;s cash distributions are equal to 100 percent of its distributable cash flow as determined from its financial statements based upon earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization less interest expense and maintenance capital expenditures. The Partnership paid monthly distributions approximately one month following the end of each reported month.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Partnership paid distributions to its general partners of $190.1 million and $199.3 million, respectively. For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Partnership received contributions from its general partners of $202.0 and nil, respectively. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0d2e82;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;(11) SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:center"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:70.833%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:58.563%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:19.068%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:19.069%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #0a2299;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="6" style="border-top:1pt solid #0a2299;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;(In thousands)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Interest paid, net of amount capitalized&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;6,877&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9,512&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Accruals for property, plant and equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;89,799&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0a2299;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;35,513&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0d2e82;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;(12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0d2e82;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;SUBSEQUENT EVENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On January 14, 2026, the Partnership declared a cash distribution in the amount of $11.3 million. The distribution was paid on January 30, 2026. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On February 23, 2026, the Partnership declared a cash distribution in the amount of $26.5 million. The distribution was paid on February 27, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On March 17, 2026, the Partnership declared a cash distribution in the amount of $25.8 million. The distribution was paid on March 31, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Subsequent events have been assessed through April&#160;9, 2026, which is the date the financial statements were issued, and the Partnership concluded there were no events or transactions during this period that would require recognition or disclosure in the financial statements other than those already reflected.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock id="f-23" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:95.535%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:19.772%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.681%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.681%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.681%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.685%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="15" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:justify;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;OVERHEADS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="15" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:justify;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Administrative, engineering, and supervision salaries, expenses, and employee benefits relating to construction activities are capitalized based on labor recorded to the payroll system. The amounts so capitalized are directly assigned, based on individual construction projects, exclusive of construction orders covering the cost of capitalized software and purchases of general plant, furniture, transportation equipment, tools, and similar property, on a percentage basis with the same percentage being applied to all types of construction.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="15" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:justify;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;ALLOWANCE FOR FUNDS USED DURING CONSTRUCTION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="15" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:justify;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Computed monthly on construction work in progress, exclusive of construction projects covering the purchase of property normally placed in service when received. The amounts so capitalized are directly assigned, based on individual construction projects exclusive of construction orders covering the purchase of general plant furniture, transportation equipment, tools and similar property, on a percentage basis with the same percentage being applied to all types of construction. In 2025, $30,673,015 of equity and $2,783,405 of debt were directly charged to construction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock>
  <ferc:ExplanatoryOfSecuritiesFinancingAndRefinancingTransactionTextBlock id="f-24" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:2pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:10.5pt"&gt;Refer to pages 120, 122, and 256 for information related to debt.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:ExplanatoryOfSecuritiesFinancingAndRefinancingTransactionTextBlock>
