    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Property Under Capital Leases - Right of Use Operating Leases</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Accumulated Provision for Depreciation includes $50,771 for accumulated amortization of Right of Use Operating Leases. See Note to Financial Statements</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ASC considers the equity component of AFUDC a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes must be provided. The Respondent is required to record the deferred tax liability for AFUDC equity in Account 282 with a corresponding regulatory asset. The regulatory asset is itself a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes are recognized and recorded in Account 283. This accounting is also outlined in FERC Docket AI93-5-000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">As result of 2024 rate case settlement, the Partnership received FERC approval to establish $2,600,000.00 Rate Case Costs Regulatory Asset. This regulatory asset will be amortized monthly for 52 months. The initial amortization will begin on December-2024 including a catch up entry for months July-2024 through November-2024. Monthly amortization will conclude in October-2028.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Charged to account 282 - $144,470.16; Charged to account 283 - $105,665.56</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Northern Border "Company Use Gas Percentage" does not identify separate fuel and loss components. Therefore, gas retained from shippers is reported as "Gas Received from Shippers as Compressor Station Fuel."</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Receipts represent decreased linepack.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service, therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other deliveries represent increased linepack, Gas Used for Other Operations and Transmission expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Lines 9 through 29 are allocated to each rate type: Discounted Rate, Negotiated Rate and Recourse Rate, using a pro-rata allocation. The pro-rata share is determined by dividing the Shipper Supplied Gas for each rate type by the total Shipper Supplied Gas for lines 2 through 6 and multiplied by the corresponding monthly totals for lines 9 through 29.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Gas used as transmission mains gas in operations and other expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Effective June 1, 2025, both tracked and non-tracked fuel are valued monthly based on a 50/50 average of the Platt's Gas Daily Index for Chicago city-gates and Northern Ventura, using the index published on the last day of each month. Prior to June 1, 2025, non-tracked fuel was valued solely using the Platt's Gas Daily Index for Chicago city-gates on the last day of the month.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">General Plant includes $955,440 for Right of Use Operating Leases</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Accumulated Provision for Depreciation General Plant includes 38,921 for accumulated amortization of Right of Use Operating Leases.See Note to Financial Statements.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service, therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing&#160; do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ONEOK Northern Border Pipeline Company Holdings, L.L.C. is an indirect subsidiary of ONEOK, Inc. For additional information, refer to Note 1 of the Notes to the Financial Statements.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">TC PipeLines, LP is an indirect subsidiary of TC Energy Corporation. For additional information, refer to Note 1 of the Notes to the Financial Statements.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">As stated in the Northern Border Pipeline Company General Partnership Agreement and Note 1 of the Notes to the Financial Statements, each partner company has a number of votes on the Management Committee equal to the percentage interest hel by the partner company in the Partnership. Each partner designates two members and TC PipeLines, LP designates one of its members as chairman. The Management Committee has authority over the activities of the Partnership similar to the authority of the Board of Directors of a corporation.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ONEOK Northern Border Pipeline Company Holdings, L.L.C. is an indirect subsidiary of ONEOK, Inc. For additional information, refer to Note 1 of the Notes to the Financial Statements.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">TC PipeLines, LP is an indirect subsidiary of TC Energy Corporation. For additional information, refer to Note 1 of the Notes to the Financial Statements.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Des Plaines project has no active contracts.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The reported rate of return is an actual three year average rate of return</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Includes $53,661 for current year amortization of right of use operating leases and $149,412 for the retirement of the right of use asset.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Accumulated Provision for Depreciation for general plant includes $50,771 for right of use operating leases. See note to Financial Statements.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The fixed asset method is used.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Weighted Average interest rate at December 31, 2025</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">On September 15, 2021, the Partnership entered into a Note Purchase and Private Shelf Agreement, whereby the Partnership issued $250 million of 10-year Series A Senior Note. The Private Shelf Agreement carries an additional capacity of $100 million available for a 3-year term of which none was utilized. On December 17, 2024, the Partnership amended the Private Shelf Agreement to extend the issuance period to September 15, 2027.</link:footnote>
