    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-45" id="fn-45" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">For comparative purposes to prior filings, the amount Assessed by Regulatory Commission for 2024, including the true-up of $354 assessed in 2025 for the prior year, was $1,666,524. The new validation requires the value in this field equal the Total Expense for Current Year on Line 1 column (d).</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-46" id="fn-46" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">For comparative purposes to prior filings, the amount Assessed by Regulatory Commission for 2025 was $1,712,346.&#160; The new validation requires the value in this field to equal the Total Expense for Current Year in column (d).&#160;</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-47" id="fn-47" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Total Expense for Current Year column&#160; was repurposed from Total Expenses to Date.&#160; For comparative purposes to prior filings, the full $1,666,524, for 2024 has been expensed to date, with $1,191,388 of the amount expensed in 2025.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-48" id="fn-48" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Partnership is charged by TC Energy and related parties for services such as legal, tax, and other costs incurred on its behalf. These include, but are not limited to, employee costs and property and liability insurance costs. These costs are based on direct assignment to the extent practicable, or by using allocation methods that are reasonable reflections of the utilization of services provided to or for the benefits received by the Partnership.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-49" id="fn-49" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Partnership charges TC Energy and related parties for services such as legal, tax, and other costs incurred on its behalf. These include, but are not limited to, employee costs and property and liability insurance costs. These costs are based on direct assignment to the extent practicable, or by using allocation methods that are reasonable reflections of the utilization of services provided to or for the benefits received by the Partnership.</link:footnote>
